---
// Live demo for Baustein transformerbloecke-und-attention: the spotlight in a
// real model. Learning goal 2 of the lesson plan: attention is a weighted
// mix -- every visible earlier position gets a weight, all weights add up to
// 100 %, and you can predict which earlier word gets a lot of light. The
// causal mask (goal 4) stays visible: later tokens are locked. Pick a
// sentence, tap a token, choose block and head; the weights are real
// (Qwen3-0.6B-Base, precomputed by scripts/demos/precompute/attention.py).
// Logic: src/scripts/demos/attention.js. The weights themselves are loaded
// lazily; only the sentence texts are read here at build time.
import Demo from './Demo.astro';
import { startState } from '../../scripts/demos/attention.js';
import de from '../../scripts/demos/data/attention-de.json';
import en from '../../scripts/demos/data/attention-en.json';

interface Props {
	lang: 'de' | 'en';
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const doc = lang === 'en' ? en : de;
const copy = {
	de: {
		title: 'Der Scheinwerfer im echten Modell',
		intro: 'Hier leuchten die Scheinwerfer eines echten Sprachmodells. Tipp ein Token an: Die Tokens davor leuchten so hell, wie groß ihr Anteil am Licht eines Heads ist. Was danach kommt, bleibt gesperrt.',
		note: `Echte Anteile aus dem frei verfügbaren Modell Qwen3-0.6B-Base (${doc.layers} Blöcke mit je ${doc.heads} Heads), vorab berechnet und gerundet. Vor jeden Satz ist hier das Spezial-Token <|endoftext|> gesetzt, das im Training die Texte voneinander trennt; ein neuer Text beginnt für dieses Modell also oft direkt dahinter. Es bedeutet nichts. Gezeigt werden nur die Anteile, nicht die Values. Der „deutlichste Head“ ist der, der vom markierten Token am meisten Licht auf ein bestimmtes Wort wirft. Er erklärt nicht, warum das Modell etwas antwortet.`,
		sentence: 'Satz',
		layer: 'Block',
		head: 'Head',
		best: 'Deutlichster Head',
		tokens: 'Tokens des Satzes, antippen wählt das Token, das an der Reihe ist',
		hint: '␣ steht für ein Leerzeichen. Echte Tokens zerlegen manche Wörter.',
		mix: 'So verteilt sich das Licht',
		loading: 'Anteile werden geladen …',
		solution: 'Im deutlichsten Head (Block 25, Head 3) bekommt „Geld“ rund 42 Prozent des Lichts von „Bank“. Das ist die Ausnahme: Nur in 9 der 448 Heads dieses Modells liegt das meiste Licht von „Bank“ auf „Geld“, in 348 auf dem Spezial-Token an der Textgrenze und in 44 auf „Bank“ selbst. Das ist normal und kein Fehler der Demo; warum, erklärt der Abschnitt „Was der Scheinwerfer nicht verrät“. Jeder Head hat eine eigene gelernte Query-Matrix und damit eine eigene Query, deshalb leuchtet nicht überall dasselbe. Gleich bleibt nur: Softmax verteilt das Licht immer auf genau 100 Prozent der sichtbaren Tokens, und was nach „Bank“ kommt, bleibt gesperrt. In größeren Modellen wie Qwen3-8B ist es genauso, und das Licht allein erklärt keine Antwort.',
		goal: 'Probier es aus: Rate zuerst, auf welchem Token im Geld-Satz in den meisten Heads das meiste Licht von „Bank“ liegt. Stell dann Block und Head auf ein paar beliebige Werte: Stimmt deine Vermutung, und ergibt es jedes Mal 100 %? Erst danach zeigt „Deutlichster Head“, wo „Geld“ am hellsten ist.',
	},
	en: {
		title: 'The spotlight in a real model',
		intro: 'These are the spotlights of a real language model. Tap a token: the tokens before it light up according to their share of one head’s light. Whatever comes after stays locked.',
		note: `Real shares from the openly available model Qwen3-0.6B-Base (${doc.layers} blocks with ${doc.heads} heads each), precomputed and rounded. Each sentence here is preceded by the special token <|endoftext|>, which separates texts from one another in training; a new text for this model therefore often starts right after it. It carries no meaning. Only the shares are shown, not the values. The “clearest head” is the one that casts the most light from the marked token onto a particular word. It does not explain why the model answers the way it does.`,
		sentence: 'Sentence',
		layer: 'Block',
		head: 'Head',
		best: 'Clearest head',
		tokens: 'Tokens of the sentence, tap one to choose the token whose turn it is',
		hint: '␣ stands for a space. Real tokens split some words.',
		mix: 'How the light is shared out',
		loading: 'Loading the shares …',
		solution: 'In the clearest head (block 25, head 1), “money” gets about 61 percent of the light from “bank.” That is the exception: in only 7 of this model’s 448 heads does most of the light from “bank” fall on “money,” in 349 it falls on the special token at the text boundary, and in 39 on “bank” itself. That is normal, not a flaw of the demo; the section “What the spotlight does not reveal” explains why. Every head has its own learned query matrix and so its own query, which is why the same word is not lit everywhere. What stays the same: softmax always shares out exactly 100 percent of the light among the visible tokens, and whatever comes after “bank” stays locked. Larger models such as Qwen3-8B work the same way, and the light alone does not explain an answer.',
		goal: 'Try it: first guess which token in the money sentence gets most of the light from “bank” in most heads. Then set block and head to a few random values: is your guess right, and does it add up to 100% every time? Only then press “Clearest head” to see where “money” is brightest.',
	},
}[lang];
const uid = `att-${lang}`;
const start = startState(doc);
---

<Demo lang={lang} id={`attention-${lang}`} title={copy.title} intro={copy.intro} note={copy.note} origin="vorab" solution={copy.solution}>
	<div class="att" data-attention-demo data-lang={lang} data-testid="demo-attention">
		<div class="att-controls">
			<div class="att-sentence">
				<label class="kev-demo-label" for={`${uid}-sentence`}>{copy.sentence}</label>
				<select id={`${uid}-sentence`} class="att-select" data-sentence data-testid="demo-attention-sentence">
					{doc.sentences.map((s, i) => <option value={i} selected={i === start.sentence}>{s.text}</option>)}
				</select>
			</div>
			<div class="kev-demo-range">
				<label class="kev-demo-label" for={`${uid}-layer`}>{copy.layer}</label>
				<output for={`${uid}-layer`} data-layer-out data-testid="demo-attention-layer-value">{start.layer + 1}</output>
				<input id={`${uid}-layer`} type="range" min="1" max={doc.layers} step="1" value={start.layer + 1} data-layer data-testid="demo-attention-layer" />
			</div>
			<div class="kev-demo-range">
				<label class="kev-demo-label" for={`${uid}-head`}>{copy.head}</label>
				<output for={`${uid}-head`} data-head-out data-testid="demo-attention-head-value">{start.head + 1}</output>
				<input id={`${uid}-head`} type="range" min="1" max={doc.heads} step="1" value={start.head + 1} data-head data-testid="demo-attention-head" />
			</div>
			<button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary att-best" data-best data-testid="demo-attention-best">{copy.best}</button>
		</div>

		<div class="att-stage" data-testid="demo-attention-stage">
			<p class="kev-demo-label" id={`${uid}-tokens-label`}>{copy.tokens}</p>
			<div class="att-tokens" role="group" aria-labelledby={`${uid}-tokens-label`} data-tokens data-testid="demo-attention-tokens"></div>
			<p class="kev-demo-hint">{copy.hint}</p>
		</div>

		<div class="att-mix-wrap" data-testid="demo-attention-mix">
			<p class="kev-demo-label">{copy.mix}</p>
			<div class="att-mix" data-mix aria-hidden="true"></div>
			<p class="kev-demo-live att-live" data-live aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" data-testid="demo-attention-live">{copy.loading}</p>
		</div>

		<p class="att-goal">{copy.goal}</p>
	</div>
</Demo>

<script>
	import { brightest, decodeSentence, loadAttention, percentLabel, startState, tokenLabel } from '../../scripts/demos/attention.js';

	const TEXT = {
		de: {
			turn: 'an der Reihe',
			locked: 'gesperrt',
			lockedSr: 'gesperrt, darf nicht nach vorn sehen',
			summary: (tok: string, seen: number, n: number, layer: number, head: number, top: string, sum: string) =>
				`Block ${layer}, Head ${head}: „${tok}“ sieht ${seen} von ${n} Tokens. Am hellsten: ${top}. Zusammen ${sum}.`,
			best: (word: string, share: string) => `Deutlichster Head für diesen Satz: Hier bekommt „${word}“ ${share} des Lichts.`,
			error: 'Die Anteile konnten nicht geladen werden.',
		},
		en: {
			turn: 'its turn',
			locked: 'locked',
			lockedSr: 'locked, may not look ahead',
			summary: (tok: string, seen: number, n: number, layer: number, head: number, top: string, sum: string) =>
				`Block ${layer}, head ${head}: “${tok}” sees ${seen} of ${n} tokens. Brightest: ${top}. Together ${sum}.`,
			best: (word: string, share: string) => `Clearest head for this sentence: here “${word}” gets ${share} of the light.`,
			error: 'The shares could not be loaded.',
		},
	};

	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-attention-demo]')) {
		const lang = root.dataset.lang === 'en' ? 'en' : 'de';
		const t = TEXT[lang];
		const select = root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-sentence]')!;
		const layerIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-layer]')!;
		const headIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-head]')!;
		const bestBtn = root.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-best]')!;
		const tokensEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-tokens]')!;
		const mixEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-mix]')!;
		const live = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-live]')!;
		[select, layerIn, headIn, bestBtn].forEach((el) => (el.disabled = true));

		loadAttention(lang)
			.then((doc) => {
				const sentences = doc.sentences.map((s: any) => decodeSentence(s, doc));
				const state = startState(doc);
				let extra = '';
				const label = (piece: string) => tokenLabel(piece, doc.prefix, lang);

				const buildTokens = () => {
					const s = sentences[state.sentence];
					tokensEl.replaceChildren(
						...s.tokens.map((piece: string, k: number) => {
							const btn = document.createElement('button');
							btn.type = 'button';
							btn.className = 'att-token';
							btn.dataset.k = String(k);
							btn.dataset.testid = `demo-attention-token-${k}`;
							if (piece === doc.prefix) btn.dataset.start = 'true';
							btn.innerHTML = `<span class="att-chip"></span><span class="att-pct"></span>`;
							btn.querySelector('.att-chip')!.textContent = label(piece);
							btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
								state.query = k;
								extra = '';
								render();
							});
							return btn;
						}),
					);
				};

				const render = () => {
					const s = sentences[state.sentence];
					const w = s.spotlight(state.layer, state.head, state.query);
					layerIn.value = String(state.layer + 1);
					headIn.value = String(state.head + 1);
					root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-layer-out]')!.textContent = String(state.layer + 1);
					root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-head-out]')!.textContent = String(state.head + 1);
					tokensEl.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.att-token').forEach((btn) => {
						const k = Number(btn.dataset.k);
						const weight = w[k];
						const pct = btn.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.att-pct')!;
						const name = label(s.tokens[k]);
						btn.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(k === state.query));
						btn.dataset.query = String(k === state.query);
						if (weight === null) {
							btn.dataset.locked = 'true';
							btn.style.removeProperty('--w');
							pct.textContent = t.locked;
							btn.setAttribute('aria-label', `${name}: ${t.lockedSr}`);
						} else {
							btn.dataset.locked = 'false';
							btn.style.setProperty('--w', String(weight));
							pct.textContent = percentLabel(weight, lang);
							btn.setAttribute('aria-label', `${name}: ${percentLabel(weight, lang)}${k === state.query ? `, ${t.turn}` : ''}`);
						}
					});
					// The stacked bar: all visible weights side by side, always 100 % wide.
					mixEl.replaceChildren(
						...w.flatMap((weight: number | null, k: number) => {
							if (weight === null || weight === 0) return [];
							const seg = document.createElement('span');
							seg.className = 'att-seg';
							seg.style.setProperty('--w', String(weight));
							seg.style.flexGrow = String(weight);
							if (weight >= 0.12) seg.textContent = label(s.tokens[k]);
							return [seg];
						}),
					);
					const visible = w.filter((x: number | null) => x !== null) as number[];
					const sum = percentLabel(visible.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0), lang);
					const top = brightest(w, 2)
						.map((k: number) => `${label(s.tokens[k])} ${percentLabel(w[k], lang)}`)
						.join(', ');
					live.textContent = `${extra}${t.summary(label(s.tokens[state.query]), visible.length, s.n, state.layer + 1, state.head + 1, top, sum)}`;
				};

				select.addEventListener('change', () => {
					state.sentence = Number(select.value);
					state.query = sentences[state.sentence].focus;
					extra = '';
					buildTokens();
					render();
				});
				layerIn.addEventListener('input', () => {
					state.layer = Number(layerIn.value) - 1;
					extra = '';
					render();
				});
				headIn.addEventListener('input', () => {
					state.head = Number(headIn.value) - 1;
					extra = '';
					render();
				});
				bestBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
					const s = sentences[state.sentence];
					state.layer = s.best.layer;
					state.head = s.best.head;
					state.query = s.focus;
					const w = s.spotlight(state.layer, state.head, state.query);
					const share = s.target.reduce((sum: number, k: number) => sum + (w[k] ?? 0), 0);
					const word = s.target.map((k: number) => s.tokens[k]).join('').trim();
					extra = `${t.best(word, percentLabel(share, lang))} `;
					render();
				});

				[select, layerIn, headIn, bestBtn].forEach((el) => (el.disabled = false));
				select.value = String(state.sentence);
				buildTokens();
				render();
			})
			.catch(() => {
				live.textContent = t.error;
				live.dataset.tone = 'warn';
			});
	}
</script>

<style is:global>
	.att {
		display: grid;
		gap: var(--sp-md);
	}
	.att-controls {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.4fr) minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: var(--sp-sm) var(--sp-md);
		align-items: end;
	}
	.att-sentence {
		grid-column: 1 / -1;
	}
	.att-select {
		width: 100%;
		font: inherit;
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		color: var(--ink);
		padding: 8px 12px;
		background: var(--ground-page);
		border: 1.5px solid var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
	}
	.att-select:focus-visible {
		outline: 2px solid var(--focus);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
	.att-best {
		justify-self: start;
	}
	.att-stage {
		display: grid;
		gap: 8px;
		padding: var(--sp-sm);
		background: var(--ground-zone);
		border-radius: var(--r-lg);
	}
	.att-tokens {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 10px 6px;
	}
	.att-token {
		--w: 0;
		display: inline-flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 4px;
		min-width: 0;
		padding: 0;
		border: 0;
		background: none;
		font: inherit;
		color: var(--ink);
		cursor: pointer;
	}
	.att-chip {
		display: block;
		padding: 6px 9px;
		border: 1.5px solid var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
		font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.2;
		white-space: pre;
		/* Brightness = weight: the more light, the more amber. */
		background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--amber-viv) calc(var(--w) * 60%), var(--ground-page));
		box-shadow: 0 0 calc(var(--w) * 22px) calc(var(--w) * 4px) color-mix(in oklab, var(--amber-viv) calc(var(--w) * 70%), transparent);
		transition: background-color 0.25s ease, box-shadow 0.25s ease, opacity 0.25s ease;
	}
	.att-token[data-start='true'] .att-chip {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-style: italic;
		font-size: 0.85rem;
	}
	.att-pct {
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
		min-height: 1.2em;
	}
	.att-token[data-query='true'] .att-chip {
		border-color: var(--petrol-deep);
		outline: 2px solid var(--petrol-deep);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
	.att-token[data-query='true'] .att-pct {
		color: var(--petrol-deep);
	}
	.att-token[data-locked='true'] .att-chip {
		background: transparent;
		box-shadow: none;
		border-style: dashed;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
		opacity: 0.6;
	}
	.att-token[data-locked='true'] .att-pct {
		font-weight: 500;
		font-style: italic;
	}
	.att-token:focus-visible {
		outline: none;
	}
	.att-token:focus-visible .att-chip {
		outline: 2px solid var(--focus);
		outline-offset: 2px;
	}
	.att-mix-wrap {
		display: grid;
		gap: 8px;
		justify-items: start;
	}
	.att-mix {
		display: flex;
		width: 100%;
		height: 30px;
		border: 1px solid var(--line-deep);
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
		overflow: hidden;
		background: var(--ground-page);
	}
	.att-seg {
		--w: 0;
		flex-basis: 0;
		min-width: 2px;
		overflow: hidden;
		padding: 0 4px;
		border-right: 1px solid var(--ground-page);
		background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--amber-viv) calc(20% + var(--w) * 50%), var(--ground-page));
		font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		line-height: 30px;
		white-space: pre;
		text-overflow: ellipsis;
		color: var(--ink);
		transition: flex-grow 0.3s ease;
	}
	.att-seg:last-child {
		border-right: 0;
	}
	.att-live {
		border-radius: var(--r-md);
		line-height: 1.4;
		padding: 6px 12px;
	}
	.att-goal {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	@media (max-width: 760px) {
		.att-controls {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
		.att-best {
			grid-column: 1 / -1;
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 420px) {
		.att-controls {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
		.att-chip {
			padding: 5px 7px;
			font-size: 0.88rem;
		}
	}
</style>
